{"title":"Bolzano-Weierstrass Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Bolzano-Weierstrass Theorem</b> is a result in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Analysis\" title=\"Analysis\">analysis</a> that states that every bounded <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sequence\" title=\"Sequence\">sequence</a> of real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/0/cb07e848f9188a9fd706d99ab6513a7d949c48a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"20\" /> contains a convergent subsequence.  \n</p><p><br />\n<i>Proof</i>: Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/0/cb07e848f9188a9fd706d99ab6513a7d949c48a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"20\" /> is assumed to be bounded we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f07944af329150363407b27848ce2fefd3d1f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_n|\\le M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"20\" />.  Bisect the closed interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/0/44064907e31ae52f0521fec6f33aea0046963443.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-M,M]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" /> into two intervals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a77ef67f80eb3f0e15694bff2ab032d7460faa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-M,0]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f12856c2421502bd82a7148518f8ef138bf48bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,M]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/8/a587e29b7d0899424f5d511c00631ace6c5d1142.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_1=[-M,0]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />.  Take some point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcbc840a4b8b98ec17d6decf2cf4ade2abed0f42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n_1}\\in I_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"19\" />.  Bisect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b267db327cda83047220f49cbb647f9cc165f1c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> into two new intervals, and label the rightmost interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/41192b5d91024dbdddbdbe3cb08b0ca3b2a98159.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />.  Since there are infinite points in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/41192b5d91024dbdddbdbe3cb08b0ca3b2a98159.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> we can pick some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/3/d334bb199a83816eb2a7d82ca0c05394797a1571.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n_2}\\in I_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"19\" />, and continue this process by picking some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d489a7c6ba74a181b598fe288d4482e6a8831cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n_k}\\in I_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"19\" />.  We show that the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1be58552fe5fa35ad803a5b2667996cb04c486c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{n_k})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is convergent.  Consider the chain\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e533ff0fc37da82371c4bde3016cd66744ca9065.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\ldots\\subseteq I_k\\subseteq I_{k-1}\\subseteq\\ldots\\subseteq I_2\\subseteq I_1.\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"15\" /></center>\n<p>By the Nested Interval Property we know that there is some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5de01a97e73f9cd6fd0020787398d81801dd1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> contained in each interval.  We claim <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/6/ed695908ebf4925988fe5d81c7ec2b05b8f04424.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim a_{n_k}=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"19\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/4/ca47de052eb3fb5454694d9bce3561ebff831a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\epsilon&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> be arbitrary.  The length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/daf809c41610159bdfe278c59d38ad079f692edb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{L}(I_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/a/8ea972a3547d6e5b8c88bc77e0110bf571d75898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> is, by construction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/1/4b1e36adea60165ccc25e6f9d6919c1f7a95f5f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{L}(I_k)=M(1/2)^{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"22\" /> which converges to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> such that for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf9b653d109b16844c1b10268122ddf3f61537e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e45df6dc94810576487cc0a00c59cd7c6d7672aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{L}(I_k)&lt;\\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/538886825e63b843f080069ea9fcaab50c0a0ca8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are contained in each interval, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/5/ea5a456ff5487731719a463d879f9a573e669169.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_{n_k}-x|&lt;\\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017075529\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.018 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 85/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5084/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11431:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017075529 and revision id 174724. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}